### Top 10 Customers by Lifetime Spend
This horizontal bar chart identifies your most valuable customers. Sean Miller leads the group with a lifetime spend of over $25,000, followed by Tamara Chand. These top 10 individuals represent a significant portion of long-term value.

### Customer Composition: Returning vs. New
The donut chart shows a staggering loyalty rate: 99.2% of your 793 unique customers are returning customers. Only 0.8% of the customer base in this snapshot are classified as "New," indicating a business that relies almost entirely on its existing relationship base.

### Returning Customer AOV
While the customer base is predominantly returning, they also spend more per transaction. Returning customers have an AOV of 227.73 USD, which is 23% higher than the $184.91 spent by new customers. This suggests that as customers become familiar with the store, their trust and purchase quanitity increase.

### Note for long-term financial success
99.95% of total revenue is generated by returning customers. This highlights that the store's financial health is greatly linked to customer retention and loyalty programs rather than new customer acquisition.
